{
  "benchmark_id": "global-multi-actor-payload--initialization--negative",
  "description": "Negative global multi-actor payload initialization benchmark whose reordered-initialization source passes RMC before the family multi-store parser engine deterministically rejects it: the two-actor payload fragment is declared exactly as in the positive sibling, but main instantiates the actors in the order [receiver0, sender0] rather than the declared topology order [sender0, receiver0]. RMC accepts the well-formed Timed Rebeca source (main-order carries no runtime meaning), but the verified ReLico startup construction aligns per-actor initial stores positionally, so a reordered initialization has no valid source-to-target startup alignment and falls outside the translation's proven-correct input domain.",
